feat(mcp): add WebMCP transport for browser tools (#25184)

## Background

WebMCP exposes tools through the browser's `document.modelContext`,
rather than an MCP HTTP endpoint. The AI SDK MCP client could not
discover or execute those tools through its existing transports.

This is **PR 1 of 4**, targeting `main`. Next in the stack: #25185 adds
backend tool conversion, then #25186 adds a complete Next.js
shopping-cart example.

## Summary

- Add `Experimental_WebMCPTransport` and experimental structural browser
API types, following the [WebMCP
draft](https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/).
- Adapt discovery and execution to the existing MCP client, preserving
owner handles, stable aliases for duplicate names, annotations,
structured results, and cancellation.
- Add focused coverage, API documentation, and the stack's single patch
changeset. Tool lists are snapshots; refresh them explicitly when page
tools change.

Validation: 647 MCP tests passed in both Node and Edge; local package
build, `pnpm type-check:full`, formatting/linting, and documentation
validation passed.

## End-to-End Verification

Verified the local built package against native `document.modelContext`
in isolated Chrome 157 with WebMCP testing enabled. A registered cart
tool read 3 items and returned $75; changing the same page to 5 items
returned $125. Discovery returned serializable schemas and origin
metadata.

